# F23 reproducer, second form, resolved upstream (fca6043c): reshape dims bound to user-function parameters now resolve in the traced scope, so the parameter-bound form gives the same gradient as the literal form; checked by scripts/run-probes. The first form (dims derived from shape() of a tracked value, probes/f23_shape_derived_reshape_in_grad.mlpl) stays open.
W = param[8, 4];
W = reshape(range(32), [8, 4]) * 0.01;
rows = [1, 3, 3, 5];
def u:lit(x) {
  "literal dims";
  reshape(gather_rows(W, rows), [4, 4]) * x
}
def u:par(x, n, w) {
  "parameter-bound dims";
  reshape(gather_rows(W, rows), [n, w]) * x
}
x = reshape(range(16), [4, 4]) * 0.1;
print("literal grad", reduce_add(abs(grad(reduce_add(u:lit(x) * u:lit(x)), W))));
print("parameter grad", reduce_add(abs(grad(reduce_add(u:par(x, 4, 4) * u:par(x, 4, 4)), W))));
